Parity unit : page:admin/FleetTelemetryCoverage   kind=page   web route=/admin/telemetry/coverage
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/FleetTelemetryCoveragePage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) + maui-windows workload — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  SchemaDriftPage / ApiLogsPage / FeedbackQueuePage do. The generated prompt's idealized "FleetTelemetryCoveragePage.xaml
  + FleetTelemetryCoveragePageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these real conventions; the
  surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("FleetTelemetryCoverage", already in
  RouteTable.cs:207 -> Page("FleetTelemetryCoverage","admin/telemetry/coverage",RouteGroup.AdminDevTools)).
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data source is useFleetTelemetryCoverage (GET /tesla/fleet-telemetry/coverage).
  The view-model reads through an injected IFleetTelemetryCoverageFeed; the default EmptyFleetTelemetryCoverageFeed
  resolves the empty state (matching the SchemaDriftPage/ApiLogsPage host-injection precedent), and the
  generated-client-backed FleetTelemetryCoverageClientFeed (FleetTelemetryCoveragePage.Source.cs) binds to the generated
  OpenAPI contract client operation get_api_v1_tesla_fleet_telemetry_coverage (no params; verified present in the
  generated apps/windows/Generated/Api/ApiEndpoints.cs, path /tesla/fleet-telemetry/coverage), asserted in tests via the
  FakeApiClient. No HTTP touches the view. The tolerant FleetTelemetryCoverageSnapshot.FromJson reproduces the web
  queryFn `?? []` / `?? {}` coalescing so categories / destination_totals / orphan_fields are always non-null.
- The web page renders every region INSIDE the PageContainer body, so the native port reproduces them as visible Fluent
  regions per ADR-006: the always-on header (PageTitle + Subhead + TsButton Refresh), the five TsStatCard summary tiles,
  the legend / destination / filter TsGlassPanels, the conditional orphan-fields TsGlassPanel (warning-toned), and the
  bottom data-state region — loading (TsSpinner + Text), error (danger-toned TsGlassPanel + icon; the header Refresh is
  the retry), empty / filter-empty (TsEmptyState), and the per-category TsGlassPanel sections each carrying their
  destination chips (TsBadge) and the per-field table (Code / TsBadge cells: field · destination · column · dual-write ·
  subscribed). Never a blank region. The client-side filter (web `filter` useState + useMemo derivations) is owned by
  the view-model's SetFilter, which re-projects the already-loaded snapshot WITHOUT a refetch.
- SI units N/A: the coverage snapshot carries no unit-bearing fields (category / field / destination names, integer
  counts and routing booleans only); counts format through the shared NumberFormatting port (web fmtInt) at the display
  boundary. Case-insensitive filtering uses string.Contains(..., OrdinalIgnoreCase) (no ToLowerInvariant; CA1308-clean).
- All 37 i18n keys were added verbatim (web key names) to Strings/en/Resources.resw as translation.coverage.* (37),
  alphabetically placed between translation.costAnalysis.* and translation.critical; the surface resolves them through
  the ILocalizer facade. The ar/he catalogs already lag en by design; the app falls back to the English default via
  ILocalizer until translated. The required key name "coverage.filter.placeholder" carries a `// parity:allow` reason
  (web i18n key name, not a stub marker) so the ADR-011 placeholder gate stays green.
- Predecessor (W1) note: this fresh worktree had no generated OpenAPI C# client (apps/windows/Generated/ is git-ignored
  and regenerated, not committed). Ran the canonical codegen `npx --yes tsx@4.22.4 apps/tools/codegen/gen-clients.ts`
  (10 Kotlin + 10 C# files) to produce Generated/Api/*.cs, and supplied the git-ignored Generated/Generated.csproj
  build wrapper the Core/Tests projects ProjectReference — pure environment setup for the predecessor's output, not a
  parity shortcut. The headless logic (Model/Source/ViewModel) is compiled directly into TeslaSync.App.Tests via three
  <Compile> links (the WinUI view is excluded — it uses Microsoft.UI), matching the SchemaDriftPage test wiring.

